Package: theRefdate
Title: Simple and Fast Date Manipulation on Character Strings
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Prem", "Lueers", , "prem@lueers.net", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-3315-1438"))
Description: Provides simple and fast date manipulation functions operating on
    character strings in one of three formats: 'DD.MM.YYYY' (default),
    'YYYY-MM-DD' or 'YYYYMMDD'. The format is chosen once per R session.
    Functions include extraction of day, month, and year components,
    computation of differences between two dates, and addition or subtraction
    of months.
    "DD" is ignored in the calculations, therefore a date like 31.02.2026 is a valid
    in- or output. That's why it is so fast.
